(CHAPTER 3: DAX CONTEXTS & CALCULATE \(Page 3\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 3: DAX · Section 3.1 · Page 3]) Tj T*
(Understanding Calculated Columns versus Measures is the most important concept in DAX:) Tj T*
(- Calculated Columns are evaluated during data refresh using Row Context \(row by row\),) Tj T*
(stored permanently in RAM inside the table, and consume memory. They are used when you) Tj T*
(need a static attribute for slicing or axis grouping.) Tj T*
(- Measures are evaluated dynamically at query time when a user interacts with a report) Tj T*
(visual, using Filter Context. Measures consume zero RAM until queried and are always) Tj T*
(preferred for aggregations like Total Sales, Profit Margin %, or YoY Growth.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 3: DAX · Section 3.2 · Page 3]) Tj T*
(CALCULATE\(<expression>, <filter1>, <filter2>...\) is the most powerful function in DAX) Tj T*
(because it is the only function that can modify Filter Context. CALCULATE evaluates an) Tj T*
(expression in a modified filter context?overriding, adding, or removing active slicer) Tj T*
(and visual filters.) Tj T*
(- ALL\(Table or Column\) removes all filters from the specified table or column, commonly) Tj T*
(used to compute % of Grand Total: DIVIDE\([Total Sales], CALCULATE\([Total Sales],) Tj T*
(ALL\(DimProduct\)\)\).) Tj T*
(- ALLEXCEPT\(Table, Col1\) removes every filter on a table EXCEPT the specified columns.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 3: DAX · Section 3.3 · Page 3]) Tj T*
(Time Intelligence functions like TOTALYTD\(\), SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR\(\), and DATEADD\(\) compute) Tj T*
(comparisons across time periods. For example:) Tj T*
(Sales LY = CALCULATE\([Total Sales], SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR\(DimDate[Date]\)\).) Tj T*
(All Time Intelligence functions require a continuous, unbroken Date column.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
