(CHAPTER 4: ROW-LEVEL SECURITY & POWER BI SERVICE \(Page 4\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 4: Governance & Service · Section 4.1 · Page 4]) Tj T*
(Drill-through pages let report consumers right-click a data point \(such as a specific) Tj T*
(region or product\) and jump to a dedicated detail page filtered automatically for that) Tj T*
(item. Bookmarks capture the current visual state, filters, and spotlight selections for) Tj T*
(guided storytelling.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 4: Governance & Service · Section 4.2 · Page 4]) Tj T*
(Row-Level Security \(RLS\) restricts data visibility for specific users at the row level:) Tj T*
(- Static RLS uses hardcoded filter rules in Power BI Desktop roles, such as [Region] =) Tj T*
("West". Easy to set up for 2-3 regions, but hard to maintain for hundreds of employees.) Tj T*
(- Dynamic RLS uses a security mapping table combined with the DAX function) Tj T*
(USERPRINCIPALNAME\(\), which returns the signed-in user's email \(e.g., [Email] =) Tj T*
(USERPRINCIPALNAME\(\)\), scaling effortlessly to thousands of users.) Tj T*
(Important rule: RLS roles only restrict users assigned to the Viewer workspace role.) Tj T*
(Workspace Admins, Members, and Contributors bypass RLS restrictions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 4: Governance & Service · Section 4.3 · Page 4]) Tj T*
(To refresh Import datasets stored on local corporate servers from the cloud Power BI) Tj T*
(Service, an On-Premises Data Gateway \(Standard mode for enterprise sharing, Personal) Tj T*
(mode for single-user testing\) acts as an encrypted bridge between the cloud service and) Tj T*
(on-prem SQL databases.) Tj T*
ET
